{
  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-9017-1",
  "summary": "libgphoto2 vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that libgphoto2 did not properly manage memory when\ninitializing certain cameras. If a user were tricked into connecting a\nmalicious USB device, an attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\nlibgphoto2 to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute\narbitrary code. (CVE-2026-120451)\n\nIt was discovered that libgphoto2 did not properly manage memory when\nprocessing certain thumbnails. If a user were tricked into connecting a\nmalicious USB device, an attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\nlibgphoto2 to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or expose sensitive\ninformation. (CVE-2026-120452)",
